WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:06.980
Part five: Hub game rosters. How to read a roster, and how to put someone on a spot yourself.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.948
Hub games show how many spots are filled, and whether sign-up is open.

00:00:12.148 --> 00:00:13.990
Tap Roster.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.086
The roster shows the game, whether sign-up is open, and when it closes.

00:00:19.286 --> 00:00:22.700
Reach out has the group text buttons. That's part eight.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:29.279
Each stand lists its positions: the time, how many are filled, and whether it needs a permit or is the lead.

00:00:29.479 --> 00:00:33.512
Every person has Move, Hand off, and Remove. That's part six.

00:00:33.712 --> 00:00:37.500
And plus Add someone puts a person on that position.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.527
A full position shows its waitlist.

00:00:40.727 --> 00:00:44.653
People an admin added are marked, by Admin, and the admin's name.

00:00:44.853 --> 00:00:49.710
Here, NW needs another permit server. Tap plus Add someone.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.401
Search for the volunteer by name, email, or phone, and pick them.

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:58.377
Their hours go to their student on file, or pick General fund.

00:00:58.577 --> 00:01:08.626
Override open time lets you add someone before sign-up opens, or after it locks. Override lead rule skips the stand-lead minimum. Both are logged.

00:01:08.826 --> 00:01:11.451
Add a note if you want. It goes in the log.

00:01:11.651 --> 00:01:15.950
It's stamped with your name, logged, and the person gets an email.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:24.118
If their paperwork isn't complete, the Hub stops you. You can still add them, but only with a reason, and the reason is logged.

00:01:24.318 --> 00:01:31.010
Type the reason, and tap Add again. A student can never be put on a permit spot, reason or not.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.990
Done. The roster reloads, with them on it.
